-  sept
'  bond: the default slot vocabulary — the well-known myth keys the
'  system writes and reads by agreement rather than invention.  Every
'  bond slot lives under /sys (kernel- and system-owned vocabulary,
'  fenced from user data); anything not named here is an ad-hoc slot,
'  free-form but unknown to the tooling.  The old shrubbery slot
'  cards ride at the bottom as reference lore.
+  bond
  '  The slot vocabulary, one member per well-known key.
  +  content
    '  The primary item at this name.
    '
    '  This is the default target of most overlays that act on a pail.
    '  /v/0/sys/slot/content
    ^  path
    '/sys/content
  +  src
    '  Textual source.
    '  /v/0/sys/slot/src
    ^  path
    '/sys/src
  +  lede
    '  A short title for this name.
    '  /v/0/sys/lore/lede
    ^  path
    '/sys/lede
  +  help
    '  A longer description of what the name is/does.
    '  /v/0/sys/lore/help
    ^  path
    '/sys/help
  +  type
    '  The type-in-the-last-instance.
    '
    '  This should be a callable of arity 1 whose kernel are the members
    '  of the set.  You should almost always never use this slot
    '  directly; it exists for namespace compatibility reasons
    '  (migrations of type of type, typesystem pluralism).
    '  /v/0/sys/slot/type
    ^  path
    '/sys/type
  +  mold
    '  Foil's perspective on a type.
    '
    '  This should be +type from the compiler internals; it is what is
    '  actually used when dealing with types currently.
    '  /v/0/sys/slot/mold
    ^  path
    '/sys/mold
  +  limb
    '  List of transition functions that govern the evolution of a path.
    '
    '  Should always be a list of paths to hands (at the %/content
    '  slot).  The behavior chain: if present, must be a list of paths
    '  to behaviors; if absent, treated as if ~, meaning the path is
    '  unconstrained.
    '  /v/0/sys/slot/limb
    ^  path
    '/sys/limb
  +  crew
    '  The dependency map: from local slot name to (care, path).
    '  /v/0/sys/slot/crew
    ^  path
    '/sys/crew
  +  author
    '  /v/0/sys/slot/author
    ^  path
    '/sys/author
  +  unreads
    '  Used to indicate that a path has unreads.
    '  /v/0/sys/slot/unreads
    ^  path
    '/sys/unreads
  +  req
    '  The request record on a driver-minted node.
    '  /v/0/sys/slot/req
    ^  path
    '/sys/req
  +  res
    '  The response record a serving behavior writes back.  Presence is
    '  the completion signal — there is no separate done flag.
    '  /v/0/sys/slot/res
    ^  path
    '/sys/res
'  The old shrubbery slot cards, for reference:
'
'  ++  get-auth-slot-card
'    ^-  sard:vine
'    :+  /sys/slot/auth  %make
'    %-  ~(gas by *myth:t) ::
'    :~  [lede:slot:t %txt 'Authorization']
'    ==
'  ++  get-crew-slot-card
'    ^-  sard:vine
'    :+  /sys/slot/crew  %make
'    %-  ~(gas by *myth:t) ::
'    :~  [lede:slot:t %txt 'Dependencies']
'    ==
'  ++  get-kook-slot-card
'    ^-  sard:vine
'    :+  /sys/slot/kook  %make
'    %-  ~(gas by *myth:t) ::
'    :~  [lede:slot:t %txt 'Behaviour chain']
'         :+  help:slot:t  %txt
'  %-  crip
'  %-  zing
'  :~  "The behaviour chain defines rules and behaviours for the evolution "
'      "of this path. If present, must be a list of paths to behaviours. If "
'      "absent, then treated as if ~, meaning that the path is unconstrained. "
'  ==  ==
'  ++  get-help-slot-card
'    ^-  sard:vine
'    :+  /sys/slot/help  %make
'    %-  ~(gas by *myth:t) ::
'    :~  [lede:slot:t %txt 'Help']
'    ==
'  ++  get-lede-slot-card
'    ^-  sard:vine
'    :+  /sys/slot/lede  %make
'    %-  ~(gas by *myth:t) ::
'    :~  [lede:slot:t %txt 'Title']
'    ==
'  ++  get-clan-slot-card
'    ^-  sard:vine
'    :+  /sys/slot/clan  %make
'    %-  ~(gas by *myth:t) ::
'    :~  [lede:slot:t %txt 'Children Schema']
'         :+  help:slot:t  %txt
'  %-  crip
'  %-  zing
'  :~
'  "The clan slot is used to define a schema for the children of a particular shrub. "
'  "Usually, this is occupied by a $soma. If a $soma is present at this slot, then"
'  " the vine will assert that any new shrubs that are parents of the shrub in question"
'  " match the soma, aborting the event if they do not. Otherwise, the contents of the "
'  "clan slot are purely advisory. Usually, the $soma will be a computed slot, being "
'  "derived from the imps slot."
'  ==  ==
'  ++  get-vase-slot-card
'    ^-  sard:vine
'    :+  /sys/slot/vase  %make
'    %-  ~(gas by *myth:t) ::
'    :~  [lede:slot:t %txt 'Vase']
'        :+  help:slot:t  %txt
'  %-  crip
'  %-  zing
'  :~
'  "Vases are used ubiquitiously in shrubbery kernelspace for metaprogramming. "
'  "Their use in userspace is planned to be phased out, however, while they remain"
'  " you should be careful. There are checks on so-called 'evil' vases, but this "
'  "can be bypassed if you use the %vase stud"
'  ==  ==
'  ++  get-prodigy-slot-card
'    ^-  sard:vine
'    :+  prodigy:slot:t  %make
'    %-  ~(gas by *myth:t) ::
'    :~  [lede:slot:t %txt 'Primary children']
'        :: [icon:slot:t %txt 'network']
'        :+  help:slot:t  %txt
'  %-  crip
'  %-  zing
'  :~
'  "Slot indicating which of the child subpaths should be treated as primary. "
'  ==  ==
'  ++  get-unreads-card
'    ^-  sard:vine
'    :+  unreads:slot:t  %make
'    %-  ~(gas by *myth:t) ::
'    :~  [lede:slot:t %txt 'Unreads']
'        [icon:slot:t %txt 'envelope.badge']
'        :+  help:slot:t  %txt
'  %-  crip
'  %-  zing
'  :~
'  "Used to indicate that a path has unreads"
'  ==  ==
